# Milestone: M3 (activated v0.10.15-vm-decomp-2, v0.10.7-B)
# Covers: tag.stop() inside a try/finally block runs the finally clause as the
#         TAG_STOP unwind walks the cleanup stack; the finally body executes
#         exactly once.  Realm.cleaned ends 1.
# matrix-row: tag-stop
#
# Activated at v0.10.15-vm-decomp-2: OP_PUSH_TAG user-tag binding (v0.10.9-B)
# makes t.stop() from inside `t: { ... }` a clean in-scope tag-stop that
# deposits TAG_STOP on this strand; the unwind walker runs FLAG_HAS_FINALLY
# bodies on ANY pending unwind kind (src/runtime/uunwind.c, run_cleanup_with_
# replace), so the finally fires before the TAG_SCOPE is popped.  The tag-stop
# scope block then evaluates to nil (tag-stop "absorption" / resume-after-scope
# is the separate, deferred T29 concern).  Closes design-risks v0.10.7-B.
var t = Tag.new()
Realm.cleaned = 0
t: { try { t.stop() } finally { Realm.cleaned = 1 } }
Realm.cleaned
[00000000] <Tag>
[00000000] 0
[00000000] nil
[00000001] 1
